---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---

<Page
  title="Privacy Policy | Checkmate Patterns"
  description="How Checkmate Patterns handles your data: what is collected, why, for how long, and your rights under the GDPR."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="meta">Last updated {site.legalUpdated}</p>

  <p>
    This policy explains what personal data {site.name} ({site.url}) processes when you use the
    site, why, and what your rights are. It is written to meet the EU General Data Protection
    Regulation (GDPR, in Dutch: AVG) and the Dutch Telecommunications Act (Telecommunicatiewet).
  </p>

  <h2>In short</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You don’t need an account and we never ask for your name, email or any other details.</li>
    <li>Your puzzle progress is stored only in your own browser and is never sent to us.</li>
    <li>
      We use analytics to see how many people visit and which pages they use. Google Analytics only
      runs if you agree to it.
    </li>
    <li>We don’t sell your data, show ads, or build profiles of you.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who is responsible for your data</h2>
  <p>
    The data controller is {site.operator}, who runs this site as a
    private, non-commercial project. You can reach us at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What data we process and why</h2>

  <h3>Progress stored on your device</h3>
  <p>
    The list of puzzles you have solved is saved in your browser’s local storage (under the key <code>checkmate-patterns:solved</code>) so you keep your progress between visits. This data
    stays on your device and is never sent to us or anyone else. Because it is strictly necessary
    for a feature you use, no consent is required. You can delete it at any time by clearing your
    browser’s site data for {site.url}.
  </p>

  <h3>Hosting and server logs</h3>
  <p>
    The site is hosted by Vercel Inc. When you visit, Vercel’s servers automatically process
    technical data needed to deliver the pages, such as your IP address, browser type, the page
    requested and the time of the request. This is necessary to run the site and keep it secure.
    Legal basis: our legitimate interest in providing a working and secure website (GDPR article
    6(1)(f)). Vercel keeps these logs only for a short period.
  </p>

  <h3>Vercel Web Analytics</h3>
  <p>
    We use Vercel Web Analytics to count visits and see which pages are popular. It does not use
    cookies and does not store anything on your device. Visitors are counted using a hash of the
    request that is discarded after 24 hours, so we cannot identify you or follow you across
    sites or days. We only see aggregated numbers. Legal basis: our legitimate interest in
    understanding how the site is used so we can improve it (GDPR article 6(1)(f)).
  </p>

  <h3>Google Analytics</h3>
  <p>
    With your consent, we use Google Analytics 4, provided by Google Ireland Limited, to understand
    in more detail how visitors use the site. Google Analytics places cookies (see below) and
    collects data such as the pages you visit, how long you stay, your device and browser type,
    and your approximate location (country or city, derived from your IP address). Google
    Analytics 4 does not store full IP addresses. We have turned off data sharing with Google for
    its own purposes and do not use Google Analytics for advertising.
  </p>
  <p>
    Legal basis: your consent (GDPR article 6(1)(a)). You can withdraw your consent at any time;
    this doesn’t affect processing that took place before you withdrew it. Google may process data
    in the United States; such transfers are covered by the EU–US Data Privacy Framework, under
    which Google is certified. See <a
    href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google’s privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>We only use cookies for Google Analytics, and only after you agree.</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Name</th><th>Provider</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Expires</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>_ga</code></td><td>Google</td><td>Distinguishes visitors</td><td>2 years</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>_ga_*</code></td><td>Google</td><td>Keeps track of the current visit</td><td>2 years</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>How long we keep data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Progress in your browser: until you clear it.</li>
    <li>Server logs: a short period, as set by our hosting provider.</li>
    <li>Vercel Web Analytics: only aggregated, anonymous statistics are kept.</li>
    <li>Google Analytics: event data is deleted automatically after at most 14 months.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who we share data with</h2>
  <p>
    Only with the service providers named above (Vercel and Google), who process data on our
    behalf to host the site and provide statistics. We don’t sell or rent personal data, and we
    don’t share it with anyone else unless the law requires us to.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    The site is suitable for chess players of all ages. We don’t knowingly collect personal data
    from children. Children under 16 should only agree to analytics cookies with permission from a
    parent or guardian.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>access the personal data we hold about you;</li>
    <li>have incorrect data corrected;</li>
    <li>have your data deleted;</li>
    <li>restrict or object to processing;</li>
    <li>receive your data in a portable format;</li>
    <li>withdraw your consent at any time.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Because we don’t ask for your name or contact details, we usually cannot link data to you. To
    exercise your rights, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we will
    respond within one month. You also have the right to file a complaint with the Dutch Data
    Protection Authority (<a href="https://autoriteitpersoonsgegevens.nl" rel="noopener">Autoriteit
    Persoonsgegevens</a>) or the data protection authority in your own country.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy, for example when we add or change a service. The date at the top
    shows when it was last changed. Significant changes will be announced on the site.
  </p>
</Page>
